 "text": "Hi! How's life treating you? It depends on the thin film varnish you used. If it's glass, I'd err on the side of too long. Oil takes ages to dry completely. That's a lot of time to let the oil dry, especially since six months is really two dry months each. You could pick up the painting from the gallery and varnish it there, just after midday when the gallery is at its quietest. That way you'd still be able to present it before weekend. Brush marks disappear, the paint feels smooth to the touch, and there' no feel of the varnish on surface changing the oil paint any way.",
